 are under  evacuation alert  erin sophie cooler temperatures today  giving crews a chance to get  hopefully get a handle on this fire but  last night bad news  at least one home destroyed by flames  it's terrifying to watch the raging fire  clearly visible to people in penticton  people here are ready for the fire  season evacuation orders  still filled with emotion there's so  many houses up there and it was just  racing down the hill so  we'll see if we have a house in the days  to come  all logged off in behind there if it  gets into those plantations in the dry  grass it's really going to spread  and this wind isn't going to help the  terrain  rocky and steep difficult for ground  crews to make any progress  wednesday a parade of helicopters dipped  in skaha lake  bucketing a section of the fire right on  top of dozens of homes  for at least one homeowner it's too late  the home destroyed overnight by flames  now is the time to make sure you have a  plan  for your family and your pets so that  you don't have a situation where  someone's knocking on the door and  you're saying  i'm not ready to go the fire has  continued to spread  the bc wildfire service pins the size at  about 1400 hectares and continuing to  grow  the fight to save homes a long way from  being finished  this fire is far from contained it means  hundreds of people will  not likely be going home anytime soon  and thousands of people  ready to go at a moment's notice  sophie erin mcarthur in bc for us thank  you erin  california's wine country is dealing  with its own wildfire  emergency thousands have been told there  is an immediate threat to their lives  [Music]  several thousand homeowners in the city  of vacaville  west of sacramento have been ordered to  leave the governor declared a state of  emergency for all of california  as multiple blazes incinerate at least  18  thousand hectares of land in the napa  and sonoma valleys  an even larger complex of fires is  burning around the san francisco  bay area and smoke is covering much of  central and  northern california it's believed most  of the fires were caused by lightning  storms  on the heels of record-breaking hot  weather  the mission to vote out donald trump  coming up democrats and even some  republicans  on why joe biden should be america's  next president  it'll be a moment for the history books  in the u.s tonight at the democratic  national convention  as kamala harris accepts her nomination  for vice president in the race to unseat  president donald trump  our jackson prescott joins us from  wilmington delaware  presidential candidate joe biden's home  base jackson what are we expecting from  the convention tonight  well sophie tonight's convention will  focus on threats to the american  constitution and american way of life  former president barack obama is set to  speak from philadelphia outlining what  he calls the grave choice facing  american voters  while here in wilmington kamala harris  will address the history being made  by including her on a presidential  ticket  at this unconventional convention a few  socially distanced delegates will watch  kamala harris make history  when she speaks as the first woman of  color to be a vice presidential  candidate  harris takes the stage on a night that  will include speeches from former  president barack obama  and former presidential candidate  hillary clinton  all of them making the case for why joe  biden should be president  32 years after he mounted his first  attempt at a presidential campaign  biden officially became his party's  nominee on tuesday  joe biden joe biden joe biden  after a night that saw a 50-state  virtual roll call  and an impassioned speech to americans  from his wife  jill biden he will do for your family  what he did for ours bring us together  and make us whole the united states of  america this first of its kind  convention has focused on made for tv  moments  aimed at selling biden as a  compassionate competent and experienced  candidate  not too extreme and uniquely suited to  this era of crisis  endorsements have come from republicans  too like former secretary of state colin  powell  even as biden opens the door to the  party's growing progressive wing  and the fact is everybody wants to get  to the same place  our country is in a very serious even  existential crisis  and we need a very different president  when biden delivers his own address on  thursday from that same stage  it will be to a party united  jackson you talked about made for tv  moments with this being a virtual  convention  are people still tuning in and paying  attention  yeah sophie nearly 30 million viewers  tuned in last night between tv and  online the tv ratings are down about 25  percent from the last convention four  years ago  online interest though has gone through  the roof and that's why you're seeing  this convention rolled out  in these quick moving segments which are  easily shared through social media  all right thanks for that jackson prosco  in wilmington delaware  well many are likely using their apple  devices to tune into the convention  the tech giant reached a huge milestone  today  apple has become the first u.s company  to be worth  two trillion dollars to put their  success into perspective  it took apple 42 years to reach a value  of one trillion dollars that was in  august of 2018.  it took only two more years to get to  two trillion  even more interesting apple's second  trillion came in just the past  21 weeks while the global economy shrank  due to the pandemic customers continued  to purchase products  online in record numbers while stores  were closed  apple shares have soared almost 60  percent this year and  are at an all-time high trading at 470  dollars a share  ahead giving alberta an economic boost  during the pandemic  the new finance minister's commitment to  a green economic recovery  is very much at odds with the strategy  out west  alberta's restart has put 