ge that we're up for  it's a balancing act that has not been  easy for ottawa in the past  and it won't get any easier under the  impact of covid19  heather urex west global news calgary  courtside countersuit next new video  plays in favor of the raptors role  in an nba battle  and there's a big development in a legal  battle involving raptors president  masaya jiri  for more than a year he has faced  accusations he assaulted a sheriff's  deputy after last year's championship  game  but new video has emerged telling a very  different story  footage from the deputy's body camera  shows ujiri trying to get onto the court  to celebrate  when the deputy forcefully shoves him  twice  before ujiri pushes back the deputy  alan strickland says zujiri assaulted  him after he tried to stop ujjiri  because he didn't see the proper  credentials that deputy has since sued  ajiri claiming the alleged  assault caused him great emotional and  physical pain  he's seeking nearly 100 thousand dollars  in damages plus  other compensation in a countersuit  filed this week gujiri's lawyers call  strickland's lawsuit frivolous and  motivated by greed  they say the video shows strickland was  undeniably the initial aggressor  raptors head coach nick nurse responded  to the video  to me it's pretty self-explanatory  you know um and and  and disappointing it's been a long time  it's been over a year right so it's good  to kind of  maybe get get close to some closure on  that  global news reached out to the sheriff's  office for comment they say the video  released  doesn't tell the full story that's  global national for this wednesday i'm  sophie louie tonight's your canada is  from saskatchewan's prince albert  national park  thanks for watching have a great night  [Music]
 

